  "summary": "Forge-orchestrator is a Python 3.12+ orchestration engine built on Claude Code that plans tasks into a DAG, runs parallel agents in isolated git worktrees, applies a multi-gate review, and opens PRs, with optional OpenAI routing. Evidence is mostly README product documentation plus an implementation plan describing a proposed unified planner. Evidence coverage: 155 of 255 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
